INSERT INTO "reading_passages" ("title","category","content","training_focus","word_count") VALUES ('The Inventions That Changed Medicine','科普说明文','An invention is something people make that did not exist before. Although the equipment that doctors use today is high-tech, many medical inventions began with a simple idea.

In the 1800s, the stethoscope was invented because a doctor couldn''t hear the heartbeat of a large person. To solve the problem, he rolled a piece of paper into a tube to listen to the patient''s chest. This paper tube eventually developed into the modern-day stethoscope.

The first adhesive bandage was invented in the early 1900s and has been used ever since. The sticky bandage was invented to help one woman. She was always accidentally cutting herself while she was cooking. Her husband cut up pieces of surgical tape, put some cotton material in the middle, and made bandages for her. The idea was a hit, and the sticky bandage was born.','被动语态、时间状语、因果叙述',140);
INSERT INTO "speaking_topics" ("category","question","difficulty") VALUES ('科技与生活','Describe an invention that has made your life easier.','medium');
